.. term:: Core

   The component that implements the application-facing Crypto API, coordinates key management and policy, and requests cryptographic and Driver-backed key-management capabilities through the Dispatch interface.

.. term:: Dispatch interface

   The portable interface through which the Core, or a Driver using Driver chaining, requests a configured cryptographic or key-management capability.

.. term:: Dispatch Layer

   The configuration-specific implementation of the Dispatch interface that selects an eligible Driver capability and calls the corresponding Driver entry point.

.. term:: Driver

   A provider of cryptographic operations, key-management capabilities, or both, that implements entry points from the Driver interface.

.. term:: Driver chaining

   The use of the Dispatch interface by a Driver to request a lower-level cryptographic capability.

.. term:: Driver description

   Structured data that declares the capabilities and integration properties of a Driver.

.. term:: Driver interface

   The portable interface implemented by Drivers and called by the Dispatch Layer.

.. term:: Opaque Driver

   A Driver that owns a protected representation of key material and provides the capabilities that use keys in that representation.

.. term:: Transparent Driver

   A Driver whose capabilities operate on keys represented in the formats specified by the Crypto API.

